o MiB of file contents, up to 1,500 nodes. Browser storage is not a backup and may be cleared or evicted.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"storage-actions\"\u003e\u003cbutton id=\"sync\"\u003eSync volume\u003c/button\u003e\u003cbutton id=\"backup\"\u003eDownload backup\u003c/button\u003e\u003cbutton id=\"previous-backup\"\u003ePrevious committed backup\u003c/button\u003e\u003cbutton id=\"restore\"\u003eRestore backup…\u003c/button\u003e\u003cbutton id=\"persist\"\u003eRequest persistent storage\u003c/button\u003e\u003cinput id=\"restore-file\" type=\"file\" accept=\"application/json,.json\" hidden=\"\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp id=\"storage-status\" class=\"fine\"\u003eNo volume status yet.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cform id=\"path-form\"\u003e\u003clabel for=\"path\"\u003eVFS path\u003c/label\u003e\u003cinput id=\"path\" value=\"/var/hpu\" maxlength=\"4096\"\u003e\u003cbutton\u003eOpen directory\u003c/button\u003e\u003cbutton id=\"parent\" type=\"button\"\u003eParent\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/form\u003e\u003cdiv id=\"file-list\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp class=\"fine\"\u003ePaths here belong to the virtual filesystem, not C:\\ or D:\\. Only selected exports are downloaded to your computer. Restore replaces the virtual volume after validation and preserves its previous committed revision.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/section\u003e\n\u003csection id=\"system\" class=\"view\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"section-heading\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"eyebrow\"\u003eEXECUTION BOUNDARY\u003c/div\u003e\u003ch1\u003eWhat this build actually does.\u003c/h1\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"system-grid\"\u003e\u003carticle\u003e\u003ch2\u003eConsole → worker → storage\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe compiled native presenter opens this browser application through WebView2. The optional WebSocket launcher connects HERMIT terminals to the same XPU worker through localhost. XPU terminals share one numerical engine and virtual volume. Administrator PowerShell is a separate Windows terminal, opened explicitly through Windows elevation; Invoke-JA21Terminal sends work to XPU 1 or 2 and returns its completed result.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe SPIRAL shell has quoting, variables, aliases, pipelines, redirects, history, and a bounded virtual filesystem. It is not Bash, PowerShell, or a host operating system.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/article\u003e\u003carticle\u003e\u003ch2\u003eCPU models and measured GPU confirmation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe field simulator computes Fourier propagation, optical gate models, phase retrieval, GIF spooling, and LUT transformations in JavaScript. Legacy “GPU” byte loops remain batched CPU loops. The Semi-sili XPU tab dispatches a separate WebGPU integer kernel and records actual readback confirmation when available.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eLandauer-related values are transition-cost proxies, not measured heat. Bloch, Wigner, and penteract values are model-derived visualizations, not measurements of quantum hardware or physical five-dimensional storage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/article\u003e\u003carticle\u003e\u003ch2\u003eData protection\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eA single-writer Web Lock and transactional revision checks prevent cooperating windows from overwriting one another. Recovery validates snapshots before replacing live state. Corrupt data never triggers a factory reset.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eChecksums detect accidental changes; they are not signatures or authentication. Keep exported backups. Old releases do not honor the new lock protocol and should not run on the same origin.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/article\u003e\u003carticle\u003e\u003ch2\u003eRelease 2.4.0\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/validate.html\"\u003eOpen the browser validation kit\u003c/a\u003e. It uses an isolated test volume and exports CPU, GPU and persistence results.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNo third-party runtime package installation. Original research attachments remain unchanged under references/. The removed cloud/auth scaffold and original generated outputs are retained in audit/legacy-scaffold.zip, not served by the app.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSee AUDIT_REPORT.md, CHANGELOG.md, and the reproducible test suite in the release folder. The native console requires WebView2 and uses the existing CPU/GPU. The optional developer launcher provisions a hash-verified private Node.js runtime.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/article\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/section\u003e\n\u003c/main\u003e\u003cfooter\u003e\u003cspan\u003eJA21 2.4.0 · LOCAL_BROWSER\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003e8 XPU terminals + 1 administrator terminal · local connections\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/footer\u003e\n\n\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e","domTruncated":false,"href":"https://ja21-silicon.invalid/index.html","notice":"","operation":"byte chip","readyState":"complete","transcript":"          ╲  ┆  ╱              Software server · hermit.vws.v3 ·\n        ▪ ┄┄ ◆ ┄┄ ▪            SPIRAL · IndexedDB virtual volume\n          ╱  ┆  ╲              JA21 shell · no physical XPU attac\n        ▪      ▪      ▪\n  ⌞                                                        ⌟\n\n  Type help · disk · image verify · poweroff keeps this volume\n\noperator@virtual0 ~ › echo qa_461765a2ea_begin_3; cat /tmp/webvie\n\\n\u0027; echo qa_461765a2ea_done_3\nqa_461765a2ea_begin_3\ncommitted_webview_value\n\nqa_461765a2ea_done_3\noperator@virtual0 ~ ›"}